<http://data.silknow.org/object/9210db44-08c0-3ef6-9b74-6e9bbe225d80/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Ribbon of Jacquard-woven figured silk. Woven in blue and white with a symmetrical pattern of a delicate wreath of twining ivy and other leaves, above which are sprays of a flower with cinquefoil leaves. The design is formed of silk weft in both colours left flush or bound on fancy twills on a white tabby ground. Blue satin selvedges and 'pearl edge' borders the ribbon.\n\nThe ribbon has a weaving fault about 6.5 inches from the lower edge.\n\nOn the back is a label showing that this ribbon was one of a group of ribbons exhibited in the 1851 Great Exhibition."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/9210db44-08c0-3ef6-9b74-6e9bbe225d80> .

